# Best AI Design Skills/Plugins for Claude Code: Synthesis Report\
\
## Bottom Line\
\
If you want one decisive answer: **install Anthropic's official [Frontend Design plugin](https://claude.com/plugins/frontend-design) + [Impeccable](https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable) (Paul Bakaus).** Every specialist surfaced this pair (or its components) as the highest-leverage combination. Add Figma's official plugin if you work in Figma, and Playwright MCP for verification. That's the consensus stack.\
\
But there's a meaningful contrarian thesis worth heeding: per the **analysis specialist (deepseek-v4-pro)**, this combo treats symptoms, not root cause. If you're building a real production app with 40+ screens, the *actual* fix is structural \'97 machine-readable design tokens + CI lint rules that ban hex literals + visual verification loops \'97 and no plugin packages this end-to-end. More on that below.\
\
---\
\
## The Consensus Stack (3+ specialists agree)\
\
### Tier 1: Universally recommended\
\
| Tool | Surfaced by | What it does |\
|---|---|---|\
| **[Anthropic Frontend Design plugin](https://claude.com/plugins/frontend-design)** | social (grok-4.3), web (gpt-5.5), scan (gemini-3.5-flash), analysis (deepseek-v4-pro) | Anthropic's official skill, ships with `anthropics/claude-code`, banishes Inter/purple-gradient/cookie-cutter patterns, pushes distinctive typography and asymmetry |\
| **Impeccable (Paul Bakaus)** | social, scan (via ecosystem), analysis | ~23 design-vocabulary commands (`polish`, `bolder`, `quieter`, `animate`, `audit`); analysis (deepseek-v4-pro) notes its dual-pass architecture \'97 LLM review *plus* a deterministic rule-based detector \'97 is unique in the ecosystem |\
| **[Figma official plugin + MCP](https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/remote-server-installation/)** | web, scan | Anthropic-blessed Figma integration with `/implement-design` and `/code-connect-components`; web (gpt-5.5) cites the [Create Design System Rules skill](https://developers.figma.com/docs/figma-mcp-server/skill-figma-create-design-system-rules/) as the canonical way to convert a Figma DS into Claude Code rules |\
\
### Tier 2: Strong consensus on the *category*, varying picks within it\
\
