\
## What the Analysis Specialist Adds That Nobody Else Said\
\
The **analysis specialist (deepseek-v4-pro)** offered the only critical view, and its three contrarian claims are worth taking seriously:\
\
1. **Convergence risk (the "Impeccable Problem").** Anthropic's skill banned Inter \uc0\u8594  everyone switched to Space Grotesk \u8594  Impeccable now bans Space Grotesk too. With ~18K developers adopting one person's taste opinions, "distinctive" choices are converging into a new monoculture. The corpus-grounded tools (**[anti-slop-design (mbeato)](https://github.com/mbeato/anti-slop-design)** with its ~281 real competitor apps, **design-builder (petbrains)** with its 405 land-book references) are the only ones that anchor output to *diverse real references* rather than a fixed rulebook.\
\
2. **Token cost nobody calculates.** Analysis (deepseek-v4-pro) estimates Impeccable alone adds 8\'9615K tokens of context overhead per session, costing a 5-person team $240\'96$450/week in pure overhead. \uc0\u9888 \u65039   **Flag this as thinly sourced** \'97 these are estimates from a single specialist with no cited measurement methodology.\
\
3. **The unsolved problem.** No tool in the ecosystem solves multi-page design system coherence. You can craft a gorgeous login page with Impeccable, then a gorgeous settings page, and they'll look like different products. The structural fix (semantic tokens like `--color-link` not `#2563EB`, lint rules that fail CI on hex literals, component `meta.ts` files with AI hints) is what the analysis specialist calls the "design systems as an API, not a library" school. No specialist named a single plugin that ships this end-to-end.\
\
